WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.279
There are places in the multiverse that human
beings were never meant to find.

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:10.509
Worlds populated with swarms of crawling spiders,
isolated dimensional prisons where faceless

00:00:10.509 --> 00:00:15.400
corpses mimic the living, and realms bathed
in the purest darkness where a glimmer of

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.939
light may reveal more than what a visitor
might ever want to see.

00:00:19.939 --> 00:00:24.949
These places serve to remind us that every
one of us is, before any other essential quality

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:28.199
of our collective experience, alone.

00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:33.760
Every human mind is an isolated incident,
struggling to make sense of every environment

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.090
while hoping to find common ground with the
other people in our lives.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:43.590
We strive to understand others and be understood,
but sadly it is often the case that we must

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:48.420
interact with fellow human beings whose motivations
seem alien to us.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:54.149
All too frequently, we are surrounded by people
we cannot relate to, in situations we have

00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:59.270
little control over, and even if we make attempts
to articulate ourselves, there will always

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:03.960
be an insurmountable gulf between the limits
of our experience and others.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:09.430
As far as each of us knows, we are the only
free-willed individuals in the cosmos, and

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:13.360
even the nature of that free will is deeply
in question.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:17.640
When many of us become overwhelmed by these
bigger questions and are forced to confront

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:24.060
our inherent loneliness, there is an instinct
to turn to unfeeling things for answers.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:29.290
Surely, the vast expanse of creation that
made us must have done so for a reason?

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:34.530
Most who ask that question spend their entire
lives waiting for confirmation of that reason.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:38.590
They reach out for something or somewhere
that they are meant to be.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:44.880
It is only the vanishing rare few that find
it - an unmistakable answer in an unspeakable

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:45.880
place.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:49.700
A terrifying vista of madness that all but
screams:

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.460
You will never belong.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:58.590
SCP-507 - the reluctant dimension hopper - has
found himself in places like these more times

00:01:58.590 --> 00:01:59.799
than he is able to count.

00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:05.649
He has seen the spiders, the room of corpses
that mimic human activity, and has peered

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:11.940
through the darkness assisted by a flashlight
and seen only the smiling face of a humanoid

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:12.940
monster.

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:18.991
There are dozens more frightening and unsettling
universes that SCP-507 has encountered, and

00:02:18.991 --> 00:02:25.660
all known instances have been archived in
document SCP-507-3B.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:30.690
Any one of the innumerable horrors that this
otherwise ordinary human male has endured

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:36.700
would send a shiver down the spine of the
best of us, but unfortunately, this is little

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:40.150
comfort to SCP-507.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:46.200
Facing down the madness of the abyss and returning
intact starts to become less triumphant when

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:50.280
it is a weekly, sometimes daily occurrence.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:55.470
The dimension hopper can barely have a moment
of peace in this life, as his irregular shifts

00:02:55.470 --> 00:03:00.850
into different realities occur without any
warning, and all the research that the Foundation

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:06.680
has done on SCP-507 seems to indicate that
there will never be an end to these trips

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.250
into the infinite.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:12.709
But no end does not necessarily imply the
lack of a beginning.

00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:18.522
The tragic existence of SCP-507 could not
have started without a cause, and part of

00:03:18.522 --> 00:03:24.920
the Foundation’s goal in containing SCP-507
is to discern an explanation for the humanoid’s

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:28.700
signature unstable mode of interdimensional
travel.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:34.610
So far, the experiments have raised one burning
question after another, with SCP-507 himself

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:39.799
having difficulty recounting some of the stranger
aspects of the dimensions he hops into and,

00:03:39.799 --> 00:03:43.140
in a grander sense, what it might all mean.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:50.030
But the Foundation has no choice but to listen
intently to SCP-507 and take notes on everything

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:53.020
he says in regards to his condition.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:57.650
After all, the phenomena of leaping to other
worlds primarily affect the dimension hopper

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:03.780
himself and can really only be understood
through a thorough understanding of the subject.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:09.190
Over the course of many interviews with SCP-507,
the research team has pieced together what

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:14.230
they believe might be the definitive history
of the reluctant dimension hopper: from his

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:19.509
native reality to the flux of ever-changing
hellscapes that occupies his current days.

00:04:19.509 --> 00:04:25.380
While it is impossible to verify, due to the
imperfect nature of memory and the countless

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:31.630
traumas suffered by SCP-507, the Foundation
believes that this record can be used as a

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:36.110
case study for further investigation into
the multiverse itself.

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:40.610
On a less practical level, the interviews
can help the Foundation to improve containment

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:47.759
for SCP-507 and make sure that his existence
is as lacking in unnecessary suffering as

00:04:47.759 --> 00:04:48.759
possible.

00:04:48.759 --> 00:04:54.440
We’re going back to the beginning: to the
earliest dimensional hops that SCP-507 can

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.360
remember in detail.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:02.720
Considering the persistent nature of SCP-507’s
anomalous capabilities, it was hardly surprising

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:07.570
for the Foundation to learn that the humanoid
did not have a conventional childhood.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:13.320
507 has never made any mention of identifiable
biological parents, nor of any grade school

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:16.780
educational facility - public or private.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:22.560
In the absence of these markers of normalcy,
SCP-507 describes spending an indeterminate

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:26.240
amount of his formative years in a fantastical
realm known as Liminora.

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:32.740
Though it has apparently been decades since
SCP-507 had hopped into Liminora, he was able

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:35.330
to describe the dimension in great detail.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:41.710
A grassy plain overrun with red, honeycombed
standing stones that seemed to sing with thousands

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:45.410
of beautiful voices as the wind blew through
them.

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:50.389
The skies of Liminora were colored a velvety
bluish-purple which never got any dimmer than

00:05:50.389 --> 00:05:51.669
a commercial nightlight.

00:05:51.669 --> 00:05:56.919
There were shallow streams of spring water
that seemed to run in all directions regardless

00:05:56.919 --> 00:05:58.250
of elevation.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:04.289
There were also dangers in Liminora: flocks
of swooping birds which SCP-507 described

00:06:04.289 --> 00:06:07.349
as having the appearance of skinless vultures.

00:06:07.349 --> 00:06:12.949
These vultures would often attempt to capture
SCP-507 and bring him to a location known

00:06:12.949 --> 00:06:14.979
as The Dawn Well.

00:06:14.979 --> 00:06:20.730
As one might expect, 507 was never actually
apprehended by the creatures, but insists

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:24.419
that these were more than ordinary birds of
prey.

00:06:24.419 --> 00:06:28.620
Vultures don’t hunt for live human children,
being scavengers, after all.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:33.910
It has also been made clear that 507 was the
only human of any sort in Liminora.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:38.580
This has led the researchers to conclude that
he most likely wasn’t born in that reality,

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:43.710
and had previously hopped there from a dimension
of origin that remains inaccessible due to

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.139
his lack of memories during infancy.

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:50.140
The dimension hopper claims that his best
friend “Finniker'' always protected him

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:51.900
from these avian threats.

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:57.169
Finniker was another creature native to Liminora
who resembled an anomalous crustacean the

00:06:57.169 --> 00:07:04.150
size of a large dog, covered in what SCP-507
believed to be a coat of tufted brown fur.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:08.880
When fending off the vultures, Finniker carried
a heavy cudgel in one of his claws.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:13.550
The blunt instrument was said to be carved
from the same material as the musical standing

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:14.550
stones.

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:19.819
Additionally, 507 has remarked that the inside
of Finniker’s shell was mostly hollow and

00:07:19.819 --> 00:07:24.680
could be used as a shelter and resting place
for the young dimension hopper as long as

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:28.009
he had the continued friendship of the creature.

00:07:28.009 --> 00:07:33.580
Many researchers who have taken statements
from SCP-507 regarding Liminora have reflexively

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:39.680
come to view the unconfirmed dimension and
507’s experiences therein as the product

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:44.750
of a wild imagination made more vivid due
to a traumatic upbringing.

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:51.139
On the other hand, SCP-507 insists that Liminora
is not a psychological coping mechanism and

00:07:51.139 --> 00:07:56.600
is, in fact, just as real as all of the other
dimensions he has hopped into.

00:07:56.600 --> 00:08:03.319
It’s difficult to dismiss his account entirely,
as no matter how many times SCP-507 is asked

00:08:03.319 --> 00:08:08.270
about Liminora and how far apart the interviews
are, the details of the account never seem

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:11.940
to deviate from what had been previously established.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:17.000
During his time in Liminora, which may have
spanned more than a year, 507 has stated that

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.810
he was the happiest he had ever been.

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:25.090
Whenever he wasn’t avoiding the vultures
of the Well of Dawn: 507 passed time by listening

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:30.949
to the music from the standing stones, surfing
the erratic currents of the shallow streams,

00:08:30.949 --> 00:08:34.419
and learning rudimentary carving techniques
with Finniker.

00:08:34.419 --> 00:08:38.190
In some ways, Liminora was paradise for a
child.

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:43.200
There was no homework or chores, and whenever
it was safe, he could play outside as much

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:44.200
as he wanted.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:49.490
It wasn’t until one terrible night that
everything about his isolated existence changed

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:50.680
for the worst.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:57.390
While falling asleep inside Finniker’s shell,
SCP-507 experienced a random dimensional shift

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.160
to a deep and forbidding forest.

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:04.930
At first, he thought this new reality was
a dream, as it was abnormally dark and misty,

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:06.690
nothing like Liminora.

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:10.160
Then he saw them: the so-called mammal-men.

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:17.430
SCP-507 remembered their chattering teeth
- long and orange, like beaver’s teeth - as

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:21.940
well as the leathery pale skin that covered
their misshapen bodies.

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:27.160
The mammal-men roared and hissed, making unnatural
noises as they chewed into the trees.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:32.839
The sound of it all was very distressing for
young SCP-507 who began to flee from the strange

00:09:32.839 --> 00:09:35.670
humanoids into the nearby bushes.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:39.930
He cried out for Finniker, hoping that his
friend would arrive and protect him, but it

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:41.290
didn’t happen.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:45.860
And try as he might, it seemed as though he
couldn’t wake up from this nightmare.

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:48.579
It wasn’t a nightmare at all, in fact.

00:09:48.579 --> 00:09:53.680
But a true dimensional shift from which there
could be no easy return.

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:57.880
Terrified for reasons beyond his comprehension,
the young dimensional hopper continued to

00:09:57.880 --> 00:09:59.640
cry out for his only friend.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:03.820
There was a sudden crack, and a loud whoosh
as one of the great trees of the forest came

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:06.210
toppling down in his direction.

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:10.840
SCP-507 braced himself for the inevitable
impact… but it never came.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:15.050
He was in what appeared to be a city now,
and it was the middle of the day.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:19.470
Crowds of human beings surrounded him, and
the sounds of automobiles and phone calls

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:21.930
drowned his mind in the cacophony.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:27.380
It was a total sensory overload compared to
Liminora, and being exposed to it after having

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:33.730
such a harrowing experience in the forest
dimension caused SCP-507 to break down into

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:34.730
tears.

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:39.190
He continued to weep and call out for Finniker,
but his crustacean friend was several worlds

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:40.190
away now.

00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:46.280
When the authorities eventually arrive, given
a call about a lost child, SCP-507 was brought

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:48.389
to the nearby police station.

00:10:48.389 --> 00:10:53.870
The officers tried to ask SCP-507 questions,
presumably about where his parents were or

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:59.010
where his home was, but 507 recalls being
unable to understand the language they were

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:02.730
speaking, and thus there was no hope of communication.

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:07.470
The adults seemed equally frustrated, and
tried speaking to the child in a number of

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:08.779
different languages.

00:11:08.779 --> 00:11:13.540
Eventually, when no parent or guardian appeared
to claim the child, it was determined that

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:16.870
SCP-507 would be placed in foster care.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:22.720
From there, SCP-507 was given to a family
that soon became his legal guardians.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:27.389
He was homeschooled on many of the basic subjects
of science and math and learned the English

00:11:27.389 --> 00:11:29.209
language through constant tutoring.

00:11:29.209 --> 00:11:34.760
While his new parents and siblings were willing
to entertain his stories of Liminora and Finniker,

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:38.950
they believed that it was little more than
the fantasy of an imaginary friend.

00:11:38.950 --> 00:11:44.339
Throughout the rest of his youth, SCP-507
experienced no unusual dimension-hopping,

00:11:44.339 --> 00:11:48.620
and began to live a relatively normal and
unremarkable life.

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:52.470
At a certain point, he even began to believe
that Liminora never existed.

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:57.089
None of the other children he knew had ever
experienced something like it, a fact that

00:11:57.089 --> 00:12:00.540
they would constantly remind him of in their
ruthless teasing.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:07.610
Even so, SCP-507 entered his teen years as
a shockingly normal individual given the circumstances.

00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:11.820
While the Foundation has never been able to
verify the names and identities of his foster

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:18.089
family members, mostly because SCP-507 has
been reluctant to divulge any related information

00:12:18.089 --> 00:12:23.500
- his seeming loyalty to keeping the people
who raised him anonymously is proof enough

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:26.779
that this chapter of his life was not fabricated.

00:12:26.779 --> 00:12:32.860
According to SCP-507’s testimony, the involuntary
shifting began to reoccur not long after he

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:34.430
had gone through puberty.

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:39.060
The sudden disappearances worried his family,
and many times they believed that he had attempted

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:40.970
to run away from home.

00:12:40.970 --> 00:12:45.470
This also had an impact on his social and
educational development, as maintaining both

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:49.380
friendships and good grades in high school
were difficult when he could disappear for

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:51.529
days and weeks at a time.

00:12:51.529 --> 00:12:55.610
The vast majority of these dimensional leaps
are uneventful beyond the strain they put

00:12:55.610 --> 00:13:02.589
on SCP-507’s efforts at a normal life, but
one, in particular, has left a lasting impact

00:13:02.589 --> 00:13:04.610
on 507.

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:10.660
It was during a Halloween block party in his
senior year when SCP-507 shifted away during

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:12.910
an attempt to refill his punch.

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:17.079
He blinked in shock to find himself in Liminora
once more.

00:13:17.079 --> 00:13:19.240
But it was not as he had left it.

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:23.820
The sky was a deep shade of maroon and cracked
like a glass surface.

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:30.110
From these cracks spilled sand-like rain onto
the now desolate plains and dried-up rivers.

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:35.100
The standing stones were mostly broken, and
there was no wind to conduct them into their

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:36.100
song.

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:40.140
The teenage 507 wandered around this ruined
Liminora in disbelief.

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:46.740
The fantastical place he remembered had been
real for his entire life, but now it was dead.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:51.899
If that wasn’t traumatizing enough, nothing
could prepare him for what awaited at the

00:13:51.899 --> 00:13:53.290
Well of Dawn.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:59.649
Near that strange pit of emanated sunlight
was the rotted, sun-bleached shell of a massive

00:13:59.649 --> 00:14:00.649
crustacean.

00:14:00.649 --> 00:14:01.649
Finniker.

00:14:01.649 --> 00:14:07.010
507 barely had time to take in the sight of
his long-lost friend before he was returned

00:14:07.010 --> 00:14:09.440
to the roof of the halloween party.

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:14.430
That was the last time he ever saw the world
of Liminora, but it was far, far, from the

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:17.490
most horrific sights that the multiverse would
have to offer.

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:20.009
Want to own an SCP of your own?

00:14:20.009 --> 00:14:23.550
Go to scpswag.com for premium anomalous merchandise!

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:30.269
Now go check out “SCP-507 - Reluctant Dimension
Hopper” and “Can SCP-096 Chase Its Victims

00:14:30.269 --> 00:14:31.660
Across The Multiverse?”

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:35.120
for more interdimensional adventures from
SCP-507!

